    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(-x)=\\dfrac{2^{-x}+2^x}{2}=f(x)$. This even function fails the horizontal line test, so its inverse is not a function.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{2^{-x}+2^x}{2}\\\\&=\\frac{2^x+2^{-x}}{2}\\\\&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$Thus $f$ is even. In particular, $f(-1)=f(1)=\\frac54$, so the horizontal line $y=\\frac54$ meets the graph at two distinct points. The function fails the horizontal line test, so its inverse relation is not a function.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
